      "targeted_symptom": "duration",
      "patient_response": "Oh, um... well, to be perfectly honest, it really hasn't been my whole life. At least, not this bad. This... this level of trouble has really only been going on for about a year and a month. \n\nYou see, I had a bit of a clumsy moment and broke my wrist back then. Because I couldn't use my hands, they shifted me into doing the shop paperwork and supervising the crew instead of my usual hands-on carpentry. I'm so grateful they kept me on and accommodated me, I really am, but... I guess sitting at a desk doing forms instead of working with my hands is just when I really started noticing that I can't seem to keep my brain on track. \n\nI hope that answers your question okay? I really don't want to sound like I'm just complaining about doing desk work, it's just... it's been a struggle. Am I explaining that alright?",
